{
  "duration": 57.699,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.14,
      "end": 2.159,
      "text": "So welcome back again. Time for one more problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 2.559,
      "end": 3.24,
      "text": "Now in this problem,"
    },
    {
      "start": 3.699,
      "end": 6.579,
      "text": "the ratio between the speeds of two cars is"
    },
    {
      "start": 6.98,
      "end": 7.159,
      "text": "three"
    },
    {
      "start": 7.539,
      "end": 8.139,
      "text": "is to four."
    },
    {
      "start": 8.639,
      "end": 11.699,
      "text": "The second car covers two hundred kilometers in two hours."
    },
    {
      "start": 12.239,
      "end": 14.199,
      "text": "We need to find the speed of the first car."
    },
    {
      "start": 14.579,
      "end": 14.899,
      "text": "First,"
    },
    {
      "start": 15.299,
      "end": 16.899,
      "text": "let us find the speed of the second car."
    },
    {
      "start": 17.34,
      "end": 20.359,
      "text": "We know that speed is equal to distance divided by time."
    },
    {
      "start": 20.859,
      "end": 23.439,
      "text": "So the speed of the second car is two hundred divided by two."
    },
    {
      "start": 24.0,
      "end": 26.099,
      "text": "This gives us one hundred kilometers per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 26.539,
      "end": 29.579,
      "text": "Now, let the speeds of the first and second cars be three"
    },
    {
      "start": 29.92,
      "end": 31.259,
      "text": "x and four x. Here,"
    },
    {
      "start": 31.799,
      "end": 34.139,
      "text": "four x represents the speed of the second car."
    },
    {
      "start": 34.52,
      "end": 36.299,
      "text": "So four x is equal to one hundred."
    },
    {
      "start": 36.739,
      "end": 40.2,
      "text": "After solving this, x is equal to twenty-five."
    },
    {
      "start": 40.559,
      "end": 47.839,
      "text": "Now, the speed of the first car is three x, so it is three multiplied by twenty-five, which gives us seventy-five kilometers per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 48.259,
      "end": 48.699,
      "text": "Hence,"
    },
    {
      "start": 49.0,
      "end": 55.459,
      "text": "the speed of the first car is seventy-five kilometers per hour. So the final answer will be option B,"
    },
    {
      "start": 56.02,
      "end": 57.699,
      "text": "seventy-five kilometers per hour."
    }
  ],
